# Python tooling CI installs, pinned by version (design.md §0.5 debt D4, §8.4).
#
# `scripts/requirements-tools.lock` is compiled from this file with
# `--generate-hashes` and installed with `pip install --require-hashes`, so the tools
# that gate the build are verified by digest rather than resolved at run time.
#
# Phase 0 ran bare `pip install pre-commit` and `pip install pip-audit`. Both floated,
# which meant the linter and the vulnerability scanner were the two least
# reproducible pieces of the pipeline.
#
# Kept separate from backend/pyproject.toml on purpose: these are CI tools, not
# backend runtime or test dependencies, and mixing them would put pre-commit into the
# dependency graph that pip-audit and the SBOM report on.
#
# Regenerate with `make lock-tools`.
pip-audit==2.7.3
pip-tools==7.6.0
pre-commit==4.0.1
